title: "sc-hop: harden data pool against DOS vectors"

doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      Follow-up to #11662 hardening the HOP node service:

      - Aggregate cross-account bandwidth bucket in `RateLimiter` — a coordinated
        set of authorized accounts can no longer saturate the pool by each
        staying within its per-account limit.
      - Per-sender rate-limiter map bounded at `max_tracked_senders`; when full,
        the sender with the most remaining token capacity is evicted —
        actively-limited senders stay tracked so an exhausted attacker cannot
        re-enter with a fresh bucket.
      - `HopDataPool::new` rejects `max_size`, `max_user_size`, and both
        `bandwidth_burst` values that are smaller than the accounted cost of a
        max-size blob at full recipient fan-out — new `HopError::InvalidConfig`.
      - `hop_claim` / `hop_ack` map `NotRecipient` to `NotFound` to close an
        existence oracle.
      - `HopDataPool::index` switched from `RwLock` to `Mutex`; `ack` and
        `insert` hold the write lock across their `meta` write to keep on-disk
        state and the in-memory index in sync.
      - Startup recovery cleans orphan `.tmp.*` files left by prior crashes.
      - Runtime API dispatch is now dynamic (`ApiExt::has_api_with`), removing
        the previous supertrait requirement on `NodeRuntimeApi`; runtimes
        without `HopRuntimeApi` fall back to cleanup-only automatically.
      - `HopError::DataTooLarge`'s second field widened from `u32` to `u64` so
        both the runtime-declared `HopRuntimeApi::max_promotion_size` cap and
        the crate-level `MAX_DATA_SIZE` can be reported in the same variant.
      - Wall-clock retention: `--hop-retention-blocks` /
        `--hop-promotion-buffer-blocks` renamed to `*-secs`.

  - audience: Node Operator
    description: |
      New flags: `--hop-global-bandwidth-per-min-mib` (1024),
      `--hop-global-bandwidth-burst-mib` (2048), `--hop-max-rate-limit-senders`
      (100 000).

crates:
  - name: sc-hop
    bump: major
